From 0bf2173fe391aa5a6582eddf273eb16e51153c9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:09:40 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] flashnext cuda: TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGES_ALL puts the
 engine's own stream on pages too

With TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGES=n and _ALL=1 every stream already ran on a pool
lane, but the plan still set the engine's own contiguous window aside in
the room (free_streams 0) and attach made --parallel - 1 lanes: at a
262,144-token window one idle window held about 8 GiB and one stream was
lost. Now _ALL makes the engine paged, as Qwen's TF_QWEN_KV_PAGES_ALL and
GLM's pool do: Loaded.engine_paged, so the core plan sets one window of
pages aside (ownPages) inside the shared pool, free_streams 1, so the
room is not charged for a contiguous one too, and a lane for every
stream. The family names its pool (kvPool), so /metrics reports
kv_capacity_mode paged and the pool's tokens. Pages unset, or pages
without _ALL: unchanged.
